Address Space Layout Randomization (ASLR):

1) The linker writes virtual address according to the rules specified in 'ld --verbose'
2) The os receives the elf file, it randomizes the virtuual addresses and makes it random
3) this is ASLR -> makes it harder for attackers to predict memory address.



